    {
      "sentence_id": 7,
      "text": "2. This is the successive journey of this petitioner, who is in custody in connection with Hemgir P.S.\nCase No.127 of 2016 corresponding to S.T. Case No.22 of 2019 pending in the Court of the learned S e s s i o n s J u d g e , S u n d a r g a r h f o r o f f e n c e p u n i s h a b l e u n d e r s e c t i o n s 366/270(2)/323/379/376(2)(1)/34 of the IPC in filing this application under section 439, Cr.P.C. for his release on bail.\n3. Heard learned Counsel for the Petitioner and learned Counsel for the State.\n4. Upon hearing the learned counsel for the petitioner and learned counsel for the State and on going through the materials on record, while being not inclined to reconsider the prayer for grant bail to the petitioner, the application stands disposed of granting liberty to the petitioner to renew his prayer for release on bail before the trial Court citing all such developments, which have taken place in the meantime for their consideration in proper prospective and disposal in accordance with law..\nIssue urgent certified copy as per law.",
